+## Simplify stage — a fully SUBSUMED row, removed
+
+A row `pins the CONVERTER case (ore_iron) and the PACKAGER case (water)` was
+deleted. Its `cause` assertions were the identical `rawRowFor(id)` calls, with
+identical defaults, already made by [eleven/one] — whose named set contains
+`ore_iron`, `water`, `liquid_oil` and `nitrogen_gas` — and its `lever === null`
+assertions merely restated `leverOf`'s first line, an S20 P3 invariant this
+change does not touch.
+
+The mutation matrix had corroborated this before it was raised: the row never
+appeared in any failing set without [eleven/one] appearing too. Confirmed by
+re-running the whole matrix after deletion — **M5 fell 6 → 5, losing exactly
+that row, and every other mutant's set was byte-identical.** Deleting it cost
+zero discriminating power.
+
+Spec item 4's requirement to "pin `ore_iron` (converter case) AND `water`
+(packager case) against the REAL bundled catalog" remains satisfied — by the
+stronger whole-set assertion rather than by two examples. The converter/packager
+rationale moved into [eleven/one]'s comment so the data-shaped claim stays
+documented where the assertion lives.
+
+## Boundary r2 — a pass-either-way ASSERTION inside a biting row
+
+Mutation testing scores whole TESTS, so a row that already fails a mutant can
+still harbour an assertion that never bites. [ui-natural]'s rate check was one:
+as first written it matched `container.textContent`, and under M5 the
+constrained line emits the byte-identical `"Iron Ore 90/min"`, so it could only
+discriminate in concert with its sibling `.chain-builder-constrained` check.
+
+Now scoped to the metrics block, it pins "on the plain RAW line" DIRECTLY
+rather than by elimination. Verified by isolation probe rather than by
+argument — siblings disabled, M5 applied — where it fails on its own with:
+
+> `expected 'Σ POWER24 MWΣ MACHINES6RAW—' to contain 'Iron Ore 90/min'`
+
+i.e. the RAW `<dd>` falling back to `"—"` (`ChainBuilder.tsx:466`) exactly as
+claimed. No mutant count moved, because the row's verdict was never in doubt;
+what changed is that each of its assertions now earns its place. Worth
+recording as a distinct failure MODE: "all mutants killed" is a statement about
+tests, not about the assertions inside them.
+
